Vertex Sample Game License

Copyright (c) 2026 BiggyStudios
https://github.com/BiggyStudios/Vertex

This license covers the game in the SampleGame folder of the Vertex repository:
its code, maps, weapons, classes, models, sounds, interface and design (together,
"the Game"). The Vertex engine in the Vertex folder is not covered by this license;
it is under the MIT License (see Vertex/LICENSE) and you can use it however you like.

Files in the SampleGame folder that come with their own license are under that
license instead (for example the Noto Sans fonts, which are under the SIL Open
Font License in Assets/Fonts/OFL.txt).

In short:
  - Learn from it, teach with it, and play it: yes.
  - Build your own, genuinely different game from it, with credit: yes.
  - Sell or monetize the Game or a lightly changed version of it: no.
  - Reupload or share the Game, changed or unchanged, even for free: no.
The numbered terms below are what actually apply; this summary is only a guide.


1. Definitions

"Credit" means a visible notice reading "Based on Vertex by BiggyStudios", with a
link to https://github.com/BiggyStudios/Vertex, placed where players and users will
see it: in the game's credits or about screen, and in its store page, download
page or README.

"Different Game" means a game that a reasonable player would not see as a copy,
version, remake, reskin or rebrand of the Game. Changing the name, art, colours,
sounds, maps or weapon stats while keeping the Game's gameplay does not make a
Different Game. For example, these are NOT Different Games:
  - the Game with a new name, logo, art style or menus;
  - the Game with new or edited maps, weapons or classes;
  - a multiplayer surf and bunny-hop arena shooter built from the Game's movement,
    weapons, classes, maps or grapple.

"Monetize" means making money from something in any way: selling it, charging to
download, play or access it, putting it behind a paywall or subscription, adding
in-game purchases or in-game advertising, or offering it on a paid store listing
(for example on Steam, itch.io or a console store).


2. What you may do

2.1 Learn and teach. You may read, run, play, study and modify the Game for
personal learning, teaching, courses, tutorials and research. You may show parts
of the Game's code, changed or unchanged, in tutorials, articles, videos and
classes, with Credit, as long as you are not releasing a playable game.

2.2 Make your own game. You may use the Game's code and content to make a
Different Game, as long as you give Credit. You may Monetize a Different Game.

2.3 Fork and contribute. You may fork the repository on GitHub and change the
Game in your fork to experiment, learn or contribute changes back, as long as you
don't release the result as a game outside that fork.

2.4 Play with changes privately. You may change the Game for your own use and
play your changed version with friends, as long as you don't publish it.


3. What you may not do

3.1 You may not Monetize the Game, or any game that is not a Different Game made
from it.

3.2 You may not share, upload or release copies of the Game, whether unchanged,
changed, renamed, reskinned or rebranded, or any game made from it that is not a
Different Game, whether you charge for it or give it away for free. GitHub forks
under 2.3 are the only exception.

3.3 You may not remove or hide Credit, or claim to have made the Game.

3.4 You may not use the BiggyStudios name to suggest that BiggyStudios made,
approves of or supports your game, beyond giving Credit.


4. Other uses

Anything this license does not allow needs written permission from BiggyStudios.
To ask, open an issue on https://github.com/BiggyStudios/Vertex.


5. Ending this license

If you break these terms, your permission under this license ends automatically.
BiggyStudios may give it back in writing if you fix the problem.


